.TH RUN-VMSCAN 1 "2026-11-07" "cti-agent 1.6" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
run-vmscan \- weekly Qualys VM scan report: the two scheduled scans combined into one email
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B run\-vmscan
.RB ( \-\-dry\-run | \-\-for\-real | \-\-to\-dev )
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent run\-vmscan
.RB ( \-\-dry\-run | \-\-for\-real | \-\-to\-dev )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B run-vmscan
runs
.BR cti\-vmscan (1)
to build the combined report from the week's
.B "Qualys: Scan Results"
notices and mails it through
.BR cti\-mailer (1)
\-\-lane vmscan. Both scans appear in the one email, each in its own section.
The email also carries the coverage check of the network spreadsheet against what
the scans cover (see
.BR cti\-vmscan (1)),
written for the network and acquisitions teams as well as security. When it has
findings they are attached as a CSV worksheet.
.PP
Recipients are
.BR VMSCAN_TO ,
checked against
.BR VMSCAN_ALLOW_TO ,
neither of which has a fallback: unset means the mailer refuses. To send to the
VM audience, reference it in both:
.B VMSCAN_TO=$VM_ALLOW_TO
and
.BR VMSCAN_ALLOW_TO=$VM_ALLOW_TO .
.PP
It is run by
.B cti\-agent\-vmscan.service
as
.B run\-vmscan \-\-for\-real
from
.BR cti\-agent\-vmscan.timer ,
Mondays at 08:00 local (the installer pins it to
.B FLEET_TIMEZONE
with
.BR FLEET_VMSCAN_TIME ).
.SH HOW TO RUN
\fBrun\-vmscan\fR mails a report, so it has no default: it has to be told how to run. Give exactly one of
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR (render and print the subject, send nothing), \fB\-\-for\-real\fR (send the report and record the notices as used),
or \fB\-\-to\-dev\fR (a test send to FLEET_DEV_EMAIL only; it may be combined with \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR to rehearse the test send).
With none it prints a usage message and exits 2 without doing anything, and
two that contradict each other are refused the same way.
.SH OPTIONS
A shell argument, matched exactly. Any other argument is refused.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Render the report, print the subject, send nothing and record nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-for\-real
Send the report. After a real send the notices it covered are recorded, so the
mailbox cleanup archives them 48 hours on.
.TP
.B \-\-to\-dev
Mail the report to
.B FLEET_DEV_EMAIL
only, subject prefixed [DEV TEST]. Nothing is recorded.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VMSCAN_TO
Recipients.
.TP
.B VMSCAN_ALLOW_TO
The allowlist they are checked against.
.TP
.B VMSCAN_SCANS
The scans to combine, by title.
.TP
.B FLEET_VMSCAN_TIME
When the installer pins the timer, in
.BR FLEET_TIMEZONE .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was sent (or rendered, for
.BR \-\-dry\-run ).
.TP
.B 1
cti\-vmscan or cti\-mailer failed, or a binary is missing.
.TP
.B 2
No mode was given, or an unknown argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
Rehearse this week's report:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-vmscan \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.PP
Send it to yourself first:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-vmscan \-\-to\-dev
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-vmscan (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-mailbox (1)
